<!--Workspace Documentation — Introduction
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.renderer.workspace.documentation.Introduction-->
<wsdocumentation:Introduction xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:wsdocumentation="com.machineblocks.bml.renderer.workspace.documentation"
  xmlns:engine="org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender"
  xmlns:render="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render"
  xmlns:mbcli="com.machineblocks.bml.cli">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Purpose and scope of the MachineBlocks Renderer workspace library
  </is>
  <documentation>
    This repository is the MachineBlocks Renderer monorepo. It authors the
    compiler target that renders MachineBlocks BML to OpenSCAD, the thin host
    CLI for that target, and the block render engine those processors call.

    Domain BML, the SCAD library, and example pairs live in @machineblocks/core
    (sibling repository machineblocks, npm @machineblocks/core). This repo
    consumes that package. It does not re-author NativeBlock, bricks, or the
    scad-lib.

    The BlockML toolchain (parser, validator, compiler, universal CLI) stays in
    the blockml repository. This repo depends on the published @blockml/* packages.

    Historical holding text in blockml/docs called the SCAD target
    @machineblocks/machineblocks-v3-scad-target and the engine
    @blockml/engine-maker (MakerEngine, maker-engine). Those names are retired
    here: the packages are @machineblocks/render-target and
    @blockml/block-render-engine. The compiler registry name stays
    machineblocks-v3-scad so existing target-matrix notes still match.

    Root README.md points here.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="wsdocumentation:PackageMap" relation="ReadNext" />
    <see type="wsdocumentation:TransferredSources" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="render:Library" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="mbcli:Library" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="engine:Library" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</wsdocumentation:Introduction>
